1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:05,358
Okay, so this morning I'm making my breakfast, minding my business, and boom. Flashbacks.

2
00:00:05,678 --> 00:00:10,080
All the stupid stuff I was doing the past, I don't know, five months on dating apps.

3
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:12,984
And I'm just standing there like... bro. Who was that guy?

4
00:00:13,833 --> 00:00:15,862
Because it's a game, right? Chase or get chased.

5
00:00:16,181 --> 00:00:20,784
You're chasing somebody who doesn't want you. Somebody's chasing you, and you don't even want them.

6
00:00:21,104 --> 00:00:24,628
And everybody's trying to prove something. Prove what? Nobody knows!

7
00:00:24,948 --> 00:00:29,109
"Hey, I'm worth looking at." Just [bleep] off. Don't look at me. I don't even care if you exist.

8
00:00:29,429 --> 00:00:33,011
That should've been my mentality. Was it? No. Of course not. Stupid idiot.

9
00:00:33,860 --> 00:00:35,231
I didn't even want that person!

10
00:00:35,551 --> 00:00:39,481
If I sat down and used my brain for one minute, just one, I would've known.

11
00:00:39,801 --> 00:00:46,740
But no. They run away, and suddenly it's, "Oh, am I not working with you? Did I do something? Maybe I can prove I'm better. Maybe I'm good enough!"

12
00:00:47,060 --> 00:00:48,902
Good enough for what? I didn't even like you!

13
00:00:49,752 --> 00:00:53,887
It's not them you want. It's the reflection. The attention. You wanna be wanted.

14
00:00:54,207 --> 00:00:58,198
And they're acting high value, so you go, yeah, must be high value. Might not be!

15
00:00:58,518 --> 00:01:03,365
And the more desperate you get, the further they go. Like a cat. You want the cat, the cat leaves.

16
00:01:03,686 --> 00:01:10,194
It's like Gojo's Infinity, and daddy Mahoraga isn't on your side. You get closer, you never get there, but you get the point.

17
00:01:11,043 --> 00:01:17,423
The funny part? I saw it. In the moment! I fully understood what I was doing, and I said, "Interesting," and kept doing it.

18
00:01:17,743 --> 00:01:18,626
It's like a drug.

19
00:01:18,945 --> 00:01:21,417
Meanwhile, my actual life is sitting there like, hello?

20
00:01:22,266 --> 00:01:28,463
I was obsessed with training. Obsessed. I had this word in my head, perfection. The absolute best at what I do.

21
00:01:28,783 --> 00:01:32,357
I had goals so big I couldn't say them out loud, it'd sound crazy.

22
00:01:32,677 --> 00:01:36,673
And what happened to them? Forgot. Completely. For a situation on my phone.

23
00:01:36,992 --> 00:01:42,188
Now I'm training sad, thinking about somebody, while at the same time I'm making somebody else sad.

24
00:01:42,509 --> 00:01:44,864
How do you even manage that? That's a little crazy.

25
00:01:45,715 --> 00:01:49,637
So how did I fix it? Genius over here got into a new situationship.

26
00:01:49,957 --> 00:01:55,500
Beautiful. Amazing. Stupid, uh, decision. Everybody can see it's stupid except the guy doing it.

27
00:01:56,350 --> 00:01:57,605
Then I got my wake-up call.

28
00:01:57,925 --> 00:02:00,853
I'd been chased before. Everybody has. But not like this.

29
00:02:01,173 --> 00:02:04,014
We just met, not even a week, and I'm already her whole life.

30
00:02:04,334 --> 00:02:08,540
I don't answer for five, ten, twenty minutes, I open my phone: twenty messages.

31
00:02:08,860 --> 00:02:12,670
"Do you wanna go?" "Do you still wanna talk to me?" "Do I even matter to you?"

32
00:02:12,990 --> 00:02:16,711
It's been a week! I just entered your life, and you're already making it run about me?

33
00:02:17,031 --> 00:02:20,956
And I'm sitting there like, what the hell... wait. Wait a minute. Do I act like this?

34
00:02:21,276 --> 00:02:27,900
Not that level. Five percent. Barely noticeable. But no. Even one percent of that, I'm not accepting for myself.

35
00:02:28,750 --> 00:02:32,723
Hold on, my neighbor is looking at me from his window. What the hell? Anyway.

36
00:02:33,574 --> 00:02:39,723
And I'm not saying I'm better than her. Everybody's better than this. Even her. Even if she doesn't think so right now.

37
00:02:40,043 --> 00:02:45,466
We're all just fooled. We watch movies, social media, and we go, "I want that drama." No you don't!

38
00:02:45,786 --> 00:02:51,644
And these apps, use your mind. You think they want you to leave? No! They want your money. You stay stuck, they stay happy.

39
00:02:52,493 --> 00:02:54,502
So leave. And don't tell me you're "resisting."

40
00:02:54,823 --> 00:02:59,705
If a knife is cutting you, you're not resisting the knife. Just stay away from the knife! Let it heal.

41
00:03:00,025 --> 00:03:03,757
But you keep going back like an idiot, "Maybe this time the knife is different."

42
00:03:04,606 --> 00:03:06,268
Put the phone down. Don't eat [bleep].

43
00:03:06,587 --> 00:03:12,506
And if I catch you at McDonald's, I hope God strikes you with a thunder. Do you know how many ingredients are in that thing?

44
00:03:12,825 --> 00:03:14,951
Go out. Look around. Go back to the old ways.

45
00:03:15,271 --> 00:03:20,091
And yeah, yeah, it's not that easy anymore, it's complicated. Doesn't matter. Find a way.

46
00:03:20,941 --> 00:03:25,742
Remember being a kid? Everything was bright, you enjoyed everything. That's your natural state.

47
00:03:26,062 --> 00:03:28,040
You can go back. Give it a month, maybe two.

48
00:03:28,360 --> 00:03:35,533
"No, my life is ruined." Relax. Remember that stupid high school relationship? "I'm doomed, it's gonna be like this forever."

49
00:03:35,853 --> 00:03:39,522
And look, you survived. Maybe you're in high school right now. I'm not. Or am I?

50
00:03:40,372 --> 00:03:46,457
You can be reborn. For real! Look at people, they change their whole life. You're not gonna be the same person forever.

51
00:03:46,777 --> 00:03:53,153
If you want it, you can be reborn. You're human, humans make mistakes, and it wouldn't be fair if you only got one shot.

52
00:03:53,473 --> 00:03:56,729
I believe that's from God. Whatever you think it's from, up to you.

53
00:03:57,049 --> 00:04:05,124
And I'm not saying don't chase love. Chase a healthy one. Loving wife, loving husband, hardworking, respectful, grinding for each other, kids.

54
00:04:05,444 --> 00:04:06,847
Not whatever that was on the app.

55
00:04:07,697 --> 00:04:12,191
Honestly, I didn't even want this video to be about dating apps. [bleep] the dating apps.

56
00:04:12,511 --> 00:04:17,660
We're sitting here like, "This piece of [bleep] looks good. Oh no, this piece of [bleep] is bad." It's all [bleep]!

57
00:04:18,510 --> 00:04:23,449
I'm talking about being alive. We say "get a life" like it's "get a job." Do you know what that is?

58
00:04:23,769 --> 00:04:27,096
People go crazy over gold. What the [bleep] is gold? A metal!

59
00:04:27,415 --> 00:04:32,454
But alive? Memories, feelings, a character you get to build. And that time's not coming back.

60
00:04:32,774 --> 00:04:36,601
You could be doing anything with it. And you're checking if somebody texted back.

61
00:04:36,921 --> 00:04:38,272
Don't waste it, man. Enjoy it.

62
00:04:38,592 --> 00:04:42,321
Anyways, don't do anything illegal today. Love you all equally. Bye.
